<!-- Exercise 061 - ControlTemplateBinding (intermediate).
     Goal:   Give the supplied Ex061_Gauge templated control its visual from a
     ControlTheme written in XAML, reaching the control's own Caption and Accent
     properties from inside the ControlTemplate with the TemplateBinding markup
     extension. Two properties, and one of them is not text, so a hard-coded
     visual cannot stand in for either.
     Drills: ControlTheme in XAML, ControlTemplate, TemplateBinding, Theme plus
     StaticResource, templated parent versus DataContext.
     Passes: dotnet test, filtered to Ex061_ (see
     Ex061_ControlTemplateBinding.axaml.cs for the exact command, because an XML
     comment may not hold two hyphens in a row). -->
<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:i="clr-namespace:FeWoLearning.Avalonia.Exercises.Intermediate"
             x:Class="FeWoLearning.Avalonia.Exercises.Intermediate.Ex061_ControlTemplateBinding">
  <!-- TODO: Ex061_Gauge (in the code-behind, given) is a TemplatedControl with
       no visual of its own. Supply one.

       Add a ControlTheme to this UserControl's Resources:

         <UserControl.Resources>
           <ControlTheme x:Key="GaugeTheme" TargetType="i:Ex061_Gauge">
             <Setter Property="Template">
               <ControlTemplate>
                 <Border Name="PART_Root"
                         Background="{TemplateBinding Accent}"
                         Padding="8">
                   <TextBlock Name="PART_Caption" Text="{TemplateBinding Caption}" />
                 </Border>
               </ControlTemplate>
             </Setter>
           </ControlTheme>
         </UserControl.Resources>

       and replace the placeholder below with the gauge itself:

         <StackPanel>
           <i:Ex061_Gauge Name="Gauge"
                          Theme="{StaticResource GaugeTheme}"
                          Caption="Gauge A"
                          Accent="#FF3366" />
         </StackPanel>

       Why TemplateBinding and not Binding: inside a ControlTemplate, plain
       Binding resolves against the DataContext, which the template's children
       inherit from whatever the control was given. TemplateBinding resolves
       against the TEMPLATED PARENT, which is the gauge itself, and that is a
       different object. The test sets the gauge's DataContext to a decoy
       exposing its own Caption of "WRONG" and then re-reads the rendered
       caption, so a Binding answer is visibly wrong rather than merely
       unidiomatic. A literal Text and a literal Background reproduce the
       resting visual exactly, so the test also changes Caption and Accent after
       the view is shown and asserts both followed. -->
  <StackPanel>
    <TextBlock Text="TODO" />
  </StackPanel>
</UserControl>
